# sources.log — retrieval ledger (audit substrate)

# Append ONE line per fetch / capture / lookup. Never edit or delete a line — corrections
# are new lines. This is the deterministic ledger the emit step audits every load-bearing
# claim against (claim-level, not link-level). No DB; just this file.
#
# Pipe-separated, 5 fields:
#   fetched_at | url_or_capture | class | supports_claim | confidence
#
#   fetched_at     ISO date of retrieval
#   url_or_capture the URL, API call, or captures/ id actually retrieved (not a redirect target)
#   class          A (artifact) | B (interface/contract) | C (live observation)  — see corroboration
#   supports_claim short claim id / phrase this retrieval backs (or "context" if background)
#   confidence     multi-source | single-source | stress-tested-not-grounded
#
# A claim may go on the user surface only if it traces to >=1 line here; 2 independent
# *classes* to be work-true. A load-bearing claim with NO line is a loud UNKNOWN.

# fetched_at  | url_or_capture            | class | supports_claim          | confidence
# 2026-08-25  | https://example.com/x     | C     | visa-free-this-quarter  | single-source
